{
 "title": "Fechas y duraciones: std.time",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "`std.time` ofrece la hora actual (`now_utc()`, `Instant.now()`) y cálculos con fechas. Guarda las fechas como tiempo Unix en milisegundos: `datetime_from_unix_millis(0)` da 1970-01-01. Tiene métodos como `add_days`, `add_months`, `weekday_name`, `to_iso`, `format`. Para lapsos de tiempo usa `Duration`."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "import std.time",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    d = time.datetime_from_unix_millis(0)",
    "    print(d.to_iso().as_str())",
    "    print(d.weekday_name())",
    "    later = d.add_days(100)",
    "    print(later.to_iso().as_str())",
    "    print(time.is_leap_year(2024), time.days_in_month(2024, 2))"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "1970-01-01T00:00:00Z",
    "Thursday",
    "1970-04-11T00:00:00Z",
    "true 29"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c10-l09-x1",
   "prompt": "Suma 365 días a 1970-01-01 e imprímelo en formato ISO.",
   "starter": [
    "import std.time",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    d = time.datetime_from_unix_millis(0)",
    "    print(d.to_iso().as_str())"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "import std.time",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    d = time.datetime_from_unix_millis(0)",
    "    print(d.add_days(365).to_iso().as_str())"
   ],
   "hint": "`d.add_days(365)`",
   "expected": [
    "1971-01-01T00:00:00Z"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c10-l09-q1",
   "q": "¿Qué fecha da `datetime_from_unix_millis(0)`?",
   "options": [
    "2000-01-01",
    "1970-01-01",
    "La fecha de hoy"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "El tiempo Unix empieza el 1 de enero de 1970."
  }
 ]
}
